1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:05,588
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:06,881
[NURSE] <i>It's done.</i>

3
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:11,803
<i>Your father has abandoned us.</i>

4
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:14,014
<i>He has a new family in Manila.</i>

5
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:18,309
<i>He cheated on me. He cheated on us!</i>

6
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:21,229
<i>He chose his mistress</i>

7
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:24,315
<i>and their illegitimate child!</i>

8
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:27,569
<i>They are to blame for your sister's death!</i>

9
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:31,698
<i>Damn them. Damn all of them.</i>

10
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:34,617
<i>Damn them!</i>

11
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:41,499
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

12
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:58,141
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

13
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:02,479
<i>Um, Auntie Pres, this will be your room.</i>

14
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:04,731
<i>And this'll be mine.</i>

15
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,859
<i>And Oliver will stay there.</i>

16
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,319
<i>As well as Dad.</i>

17
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:11,488
<i>You're letting your father</i>
<i>live here with us?</i>

18
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:15,325
[BILLY] <i>What he did to my brother</i>
<i>and me isn't easy to forget.</i>

19
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:20,622
<i>But I also can't forget</i>
<i>what he did for us.</i>

20
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,875
<i>Look at this.</i>

21
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:25,794
<i>I had this printed myself!</i>

22
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:27,295
<i>Looks good, huh?</i>

23
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:29,964
<i>Before, we used to just be</i>
<i>together in photos.</i>

24
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,592
<i>Now, we really are together!</i>

25
00:01:32,675 --> 00:01:35,678
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

26
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:36,805
<i>Pa?</i>

27
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:43,603
- [MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [ENRICO CRYING]

28
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:47,232
<i>Pa?</i>

29
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:54,030
- [MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [ENRICO KEEPS CRYING]

30
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:05,125
<i>Thank you.</i>

31
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:09,671
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

32
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:16,219
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

33
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:29,482
<i>I found these.</i>

34
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:31,818
<i>I've read all of them too.</i>

35
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:36,489
<i>Those were for every year</i>

36
00:02:37,115 --> 00:02:39,033
<i>that I couldn't be with you, Billy.</i>

37
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:43,621
<i>Would it be okay if I asked for a hug?</i>

38
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:50,837
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

39
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:11,482
[SOBBING]

40
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,033
Ma.

41
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:24,871
No matter what happens,

42
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,999
don't tell them

43
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:31,461
that you know
they're Papa's second family.

44
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:33,504
Why not?

45
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:35,423
That's the truth.

46
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,050
Ma.

47
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:39,844
Please listen to me.

48
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:44,307
That's a strong motive.

49
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:48,228
It'll just prove that you're going after
Papa's illegitimate child.

50
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:50,563
We'll get into more trouble.

51
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:53,441
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:54,400
But

53
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:57,862
shouldn't they be the ones to suffer?

54
00:03:57,946 --> 00:03:58,988
Right?

55
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:01,532
Not us.

56
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:04,202
Especially not you.

57
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:07,789
I'm sorry.

58
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:10,291
I'm sorry I dragged you into this.

59
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:11,417
[SNIFFLES]

60
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:13,836
I never meant for this to happen.

61
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:18,800
But when I saw their house burning down,

62
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:22,804
I thought that they deserved it.

63
00:04:22,887 --> 00:04:25,515
So they could go through
what happened to us.

64
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:27,392
What happened to your sister.

65
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:33,189
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

66
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:34,941
But it's also my fault, Ma.

67
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,195
I was followed. [CLICKS TONGUE]

68
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,782
They tracked us down,

69
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:44,409
and now look where we are.

70
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,579
Behind bars.

71
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:55,169
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:56,671
I will do everything possible, Ma.

73
00:04:59,507 --> 00:05:02,093
I will do everything I can
to get you out of here.

74
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,597
Not just me.

75
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:09,392
Both of us.

76
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:13,313
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:14,314
Both of us.

78
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:15,648
[SNIFFLES]

79
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:18,693
[SNIFFLES]

80
00:05:18,776 --> 00:05:25,783
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:36,794
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:19,462
[PAPER RUSTLING]

83
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:32,600
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:35,686
DAILY NEWS
FIRE BURNS DOWN HOME

85
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:45,655
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:04,298
<i>Sir Enrico.</i>

87
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:06,634
<i>I'm Private Investigator Jimenez.</i>

88
00:07:07,677 --> 00:07:08,678
<i>Uh…</i>

89
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,472
<i>Have you found my wife and daughters?</i>

90
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:15,601
<i>I'm afraid I have some bad news.</i>

91
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:19,730
<i>Your eldest daughter, Abigail?</i>

92
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:24,026
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,987
<i>She died in a fire.</i>

94
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:28,197
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:33,035
FIRE BURNS DOWN HOME

96
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:42,587
<i>How are Mariela and Bea doing?</i>

97
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,839
<i>What happened to them?</i>

98
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:48,217
<i>As for Mariela,</i>

99
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:51,220
<i>she was taken to a mental institution</i>

100
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:53,598
<i>and got confined there for years.</i>

101
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:55,558
<i>Bea had her discharged.</i>

102
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:59,020
<i>After that, there's been no news</i>
<i>or information about them I could find.</i>

103
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:06,110
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

104
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:12,158
<i>Where is my eldest daughter buried?</i>

105
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:18,498
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

106
00:08:21,375 --> 00:08:22,460
[ENRICO EXHALES SHARPLY]

107
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:26,756
<i>Abi, dear…</i>

108
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:30,384
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

109
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:34,096
<i>I wasn't a good father to you and Bea.</i>

110
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,142
<i>I promise…</i>

111
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:42,855
<i>I will find your mother and sister.</i>

112
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:49,904
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

113
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:57,453
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

114
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,996
[ENRICO] Please forgive me, Olive.

115
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,917
I wasn't with you when you
gave birth to Oliver.

116
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,419
You know, I've always wondered,

117
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:09,340
"What if you'd been there
the night Oliver was born?"

118
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:14,053
"Would Mama still be alive?"

119
00:09:14,136 --> 00:09:16,347
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,849
I was so afraid back then.

121
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:25,773
- [THUNDER RUMBLING]
- [RAIN POURING]

122
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:30,236
It was just me and Mama,

123
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,613
and no one helped us.

124
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:36,909
I kept praying for you to come.

125
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,537
I badly wished you were there.

126
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:46,627
Because I knew that if you were there,

127
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,546
you wouldn't abandon us.

128
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:54,427
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:57,305
But my prayer didn't work.

130
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:02,685
You didn't come.

131
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:10,109
I was helpless.

132
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:13,112
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:14,989
I'm sorry.

134
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:18,868
[ENRICO SOBBING]

135
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:23,039
I hope you can all forgive me.

136
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:26,334
[ENRICO BREATHES DEEPLY]

137
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,587
[ENRICO SNIFFLES, SOBS]

138
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:33,674
[ENRICO SOBS, SNIFFLES]

139
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:41,140
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [ENRICO SOBBING]

140
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:09,126
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:11:17,843 --> 00:11:20,012
I don't know if Billy will ever
be able to forgive me

142
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:21,847
for what I'm about to tell her.

143
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:24,016
I know this is too much.

144
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,811
But she needs to know the truth.

145
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:33,651
[DETERMINED MUSIC PLAYING]

146
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:45,121
[KEYS JINGLE]

147
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:50,584
[DETERMINED MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:53,796
Attorney, my mother can't stay here long.

149
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:56,757
She tried to take
her own life in the past.

150
00:11:57,758 --> 00:11:59,844
What if she does it here too?

151
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:05,057
Are you saying your mother has
a history of mental distress?

152
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:09,895
Yes. Why?

153
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:14,275
That's no guarantee she won't go to jail.

154
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:17,278
The evidence against her is strong.

155
00:12:17,361 --> 00:12:21,240
But we can argue
she wasn't in her right mind.

156
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:24,535
It could be a mitigating factor
for her penalty.

157
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:27,204
Her sentence might even be reduced.

158
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:30,583
And in some cases,

159
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:35,463
the judge orders treatment
instead of prison time.

160
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:42,470
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:47,600
What about me?

162
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:52,271
What can I do
to get out of here, Attorney?

163
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:54,190
[MUSIC BECOMES UNEASY]

164
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:57,359
Multiple charges were
filed against you by Benilda Cariño.

165
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:03,532
One way to approach this is
through amicable settlement.

166
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:06,577
[INHALES SHARPLY] What is
an amicable settlement?

167
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:08,579
Please explain it to me.

168
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:12,208
Aside from paying the damages
and signing an agreement,

169
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:15,753
you need to apologize to the victim.

170
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:20,925
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:22,301
Apologize?

172
00:13:23,385 --> 00:13:25,262
Me, apologize?

173
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:27,389
I should apologize?!

174
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:29,975
I will never apologize to that woman!

175
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:32,228
That viper! Me, really?!

176
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,480
She's the one who should apologize to me!

177
00:13:34,563 --> 00:13:37,775
She should apologize to me and my mother!

178
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,944
Bea, calm down.

179
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:44,448
For me to help you properly,

180
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:49,954
you need to tell me why
you're so angry at Ms. Cariño.

181
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:54,375
Everything you tell me is confidential.

182
00:13:56,168 --> 00:13:58,587
What really happened?

183
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:02,716
[OMINOUS MUSIC SWELLS, THEN FADES]

184
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,843
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

185
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:08,430
Billy, are you sure you're ready?

186
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,808
We don't really have a choice.

187
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,687
LoveList can't afford to slow down now.

188
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:17,982
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

189
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:24,655
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:25,990
[BILLY] Team…

191
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:29,869
I know I've been away for a few days,

192
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:33,372
so thank you for holding the fort
while I was gone.

193
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:36,667
Anyway, we have a lot to cover today.

194
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:39,712
Possible investors, um…

195
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:44,466
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

196
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:47,386
Expansion of LoveList, um…

197
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:52,641
Um… cybersecurity updates,
and competitors report.

198
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:53,726
Right.

199
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:55,102
So to start,

200
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:58,230
Claire Fabrizio
has officially expressed her interest

201
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:01,275
in investing
in LoveList's global expansion.

202
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:03,611
Claire Fabrizio?

203
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,237
Peter's wife?

204
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:10,367
Ex-wife soon, apparently.

205
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:13,704
Anyway, she's the first one
to show interest in us,

206
00:15:13,787 --> 00:15:19,793
so if she likes our projections
and presentation,

207
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:22,379
we still have a chance to close the deal.

208
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:25,674
And she also filed for divorce from Peter.

209
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:31,096
So all our firm correspondence
will go straight to Claire.

210
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,683
Mm-hmm. She's divorcing him?

211
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,727
Good for her, as she should.

212
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:41,523
Mm-hmm. And hopefully,
their investment goes through.

213
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:44,318
Well, we just need
to revise the presentation,

214
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:47,780
reflecting all the adjustments made
to the cybersecurity rollout.

215
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:50,074
Let's coordinate Jordan on that.

216
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,492
Okay.

217
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:56,705
Toni, I need solid numbers
on projected ROI,

218
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:58,749
revenue growth forecast,

219
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:03,295
and how fast we can recover
operational costs

220
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,923
once we start with the expansion.

221
00:16:06,006 --> 00:16:07,424
Yes, chief.

222
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,927
Jumping in on the budget discussion,

223
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:12,346
I'll also present the projected cost

224
00:16:12,429 --> 00:16:15,557
for our new security upgrades.

225
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:20,312
Metal scanners,
dedicated LoveLine holding areas,

226
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:23,190
additional security personnel…

227
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,651
How bad are the numbers?

228
00:16:26,568 --> 00:16:27,611
Honestly,

229
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:31,240
they are pretty high, chief.

230
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:35,077
Then we really don't have a choice.

231
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:38,038
We need to close this deal
with Claire Fabrizio.

232
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:39,039
Okay?

233
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:41,500
Okay.

234
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:45,004
[TONI] Yes.

235
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:49,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:51,343
[PHONE CHIMES]

237
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:57,099
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:00,394
I LOVE YOU, BABE. GO EAT.

239
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:06,734
WE JUST FINISHED DINNER, BABE.
I LOVE YOU TOO.

240
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:11,780
- [ROWENA] We rarely hang out.
- [RALPH] It's great here, babe.

241
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:13,240
- [CHARM] Really?
- [RALPH] Yup.

242
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:15,451
They have the best steak and…

243
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:18,037
[LOUNGE MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,496
Should we go somewhere else? Yeah?

245
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:21,415
Ralph! Son.

246
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:25,502
[ROWENA] Ralph, hi!

247
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:26,879
Come, come.

248
00:17:28,505 --> 00:17:29,381
My son.

249
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:33,552
Say hi to your aunties.

250
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:35,554
- Ah…
- [ROWENA] My son, Ralph.

251
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:36,764
Hello.

252
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,641
I heard the news.

253
00:17:40,976 --> 00:17:43,062
They caught the person ruining LoveList,

254
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:48,192
and the mom who set fire to Billy's house?

255
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:52,321
The drama of that company, it never ends.

256
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:55,240
Ma, please. Come on.

257
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:59,578
I told you, it's a mess there.

258
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:03,290
That company is bound to fail
sooner or later.

259
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:05,292
Get out while you still can.

260
00:18:05,375 --> 00:18:09,880
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

261
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:11,256
- [SETS GLASS DOWN]
- Okay.

262
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:15,552
You know I just want
what's best for you, son.

263
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,180
What's best for me?

264
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:20,849
What's best for me

265
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:24,770
is for you to stop controlling
all my decisions.

266
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:27,606
Wow.

267
00:18:28,982 --> 00:18:30,484
You don't get it, do you?

268
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:34,279
I'm doing all this for your sake.

269
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:37,658
For your future.

270
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:41,453
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:43,789
[WHISPERS] Babe, let's go?

272
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,250
Excuse us.

273
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:51,046
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

274
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:52,631
Ma.

275
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,008
I spoke with the lawyer.

276
00:18:55,592 --> 00:18:59,054
She said it's possible
you'll be moved to a hospital.

277
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,682
Isn't that great, Ma?

278
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:04,476
You won't rot here anymore.

279
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,936
You can get out.

280
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,771
Which hospital?

281
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:11,441
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:13,026
The…

283
00:19:15,654 --> 00:19:16,655
ward.

284
00:19:16,738 --> 00:19:19,283
- Crazy. She's going to a psych ward.
- [MARIELA] Wait, the psych ward?

285
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:21,118
- What am I, crazy?
- [LAUGHS] She admitted it.

286
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,245
You want to be away from me, right?

287
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:25,330
- [WOMAN] It came from her.
- Ma, no. You're not crazy.

288
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:30,169
Ma, just think about it.
You'll be better off there.

289
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,129
You'll be taken care of.

290
00:19:32,212 --> 00:19:34,173
Turns out she really is crazy.

291
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:36,175
- [WOMEN CACKLING]
- She belongs there.

292
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:37,926
- Hey!
- Ma. Hey, Ma!

293
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,553
- Let go of me! Ouch!
- Stop it, Ma!

294
00:19:39,636 --> 00:19:41,388
- [WOMAN] Stay out of this!
- [BEA] What the hell?!

295
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:43,557
- Stop it!
- Ma! Ma!

296
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:47,060
- [GRUNTS SOFTLY]
- Ma!

297
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:51,565
- Miss! Miss, help! Help!
- [WOMAN] Hey! Hey! Hey!

298
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:53,567
- Hey! What's going on there?!
- Hey! Here she comes!

299
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:55,569
[WOMAN] They started it! They're psychos!

300
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:57,487
Stop it! Quiet down!

301
00:19:57,571 --> 00:20:00,741
My mother needs a doctor!
Miss, call a doctor!

302
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,784
My mother needs one now!

303
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:09,791
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,637
[YANI] <i>Toni said it was just going to be</i>
<i>you two celebrating.</i>

305
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,596
<i>What happened?</i>

306
00:20:22,679 --> 00:20:24,556
[RALPH] <i>We wanted to celebrate</i>
<i>with you guys.</i>

307
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,892
<i>It's more fun to celebrate</i>
<i>with friends, right?</i>

308
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:30,646
<i>- Billy.</i>
<i>- This is about Charm and Ralph.</i>

309
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:32,022
<i>Let's stop stressing out.</i>

310
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:33,941
<i>You want me to get sent</i>
<i>to the mental hospital.</i>

311
00:20:34,024 --> 00:20:36,443
<i>I don't want to! I don't want to!</i>

312
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:38,445
[DINO] <i>What do you want?</i>

313
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:39,738
<i>I know about your plan.</i>

314
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:41,448
[DINO] <i>Keep your mouth shut.</i>

315
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,492
<i>Let me join your group.</i>

316
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:44,785
<i>I know someone.</i>

317
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:47,996
<i>He can give us new names</i>

318
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,206
<i>and a new life.</i>

319
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,833
[CHARM] <i>Just fix your relationship</i>
<i>with your mom first.</i>

320
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:55,087
<i>Just look at Billy.</i>
<i>She chose to forgive.</i>

321
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,339
[RALPH] <i>Can you, like,</i>
<i>honestly say that,</i>

322
00:20:57,422 --> 00:20:58,840
<i>you know, things are</i>
<i>getting better?</i>

323
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:03,220
<i>♪ My heart won't be lost ♪</i>

324
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:06,890
<i>♪ Even if you let go, I'll come back ♪</i>

325
00:21:08,684 --> 00:21:09,977
[JORDAN] <i>I thought</i>
<i>you went home?</i>

326
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,645
<i>I just wanted to ask something.</i>

327
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,605
<i>What is it?</i>

328
00:21:14,189 --> 00:21:15,649
<i>Are we okay?</i>

329
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:16,942
<i>What do you mean?</i>

330
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:18,610
<i>There's something you're not telling me.</i>
